{
  "id": "ep031",
  "duration": 55.108,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.236,
      "text": "A postage stamp declaring Pluto unexplored inspired a spacecraft to visit it.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Pluto-01 Stern 03 Pluto Color TXT.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA / Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory / Southwest Research Institute",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pluto-01_Stern_03_Pluto_Color_TXT.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.6,
          "end": 5.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.236,
      "end": 12.931,
      "text": "In 1991, the postal service released stamps showing every planet alongside its visitor except the ninth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "United States Postal Service Truck.jpg",
        "credit": "Alexander Marks (aomarks)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_Postal_Service_Truck.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.233,
          "end": 12.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.931,
      "end": 16.751,
      "text": "The Pluto stamp simply read, Pluto: Not Yet Explored.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "United States Postal Service Truck.jpg",
        "credit": "Alexander Marks (aomarks)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_Postal_Service_Truck.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.933,
          "end": 16.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.751,
      "end": 21.721,
      "text": "The phrase irked scientists so much it became a call to arms for a new mission.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "La NASA en la Embajada (34142640202).jpg",
        "credit": "Embajada de los Estados Unidos en Uruguay from Montevideo, Uruguay",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_NASA_en_la_Embajada_(34142640202).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.767,
          "end": 19.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.567,
          "end": 21.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.721,
      "end": 29.066,
      "text": "On January 19, 2006, New Horizons launched as the fastest object ever sent from Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlas V 551 launches with New Horizons.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Ken Thornsley",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_V_551_launches_with_New_Horizons.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.733,
          "end": 26.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 26.333,
          "end": 29.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.066,
      "end": 36.236,
      "text": "A Jupiter gravity assist shaved three years off the voyage, sending the probe speeding toward the outer solar system.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Jupiter&Io.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory/Southwest Research Institute/Goddard Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jupiter%26Io.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.067,
          "end": 31.8,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 36.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.236,
      "end": 43.231,
      "text": "On July 14, 2015, the spacecraft finally completed its historic close flyby of Pluto.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NH-PlutoCharon-Color-NewHorizons-20150711.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA-JHUAPL-SWRI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NH-PlutoCharon-Color-NewHorizons-20150711.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.233,
          "end": 43.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.231,
      "end": 49.856,
      "text": "Hidden onboard was that exact 1991 stamp, finally delivered to its destination.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "15-011a-NewHorizons-PlutoFlyby-ArtistConcept-14July2015-20150115.jpg",
        "credit": "Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory/Southwest Research Institute",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:15-011a-NewHorizons-PlutoFlyby-ArtistConcept-14July2015-20150115.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
